I have a complete picture. I confirmed there is no address-normalization class yet (only telephone and email normalizers exist), which is notable given the acceptance tests expect it. Here is my thorough report.

## 1. Owner entity/model class

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`**

`Owner extends Person`. Relevant fields with validation annotations:

```java
@Column(name = "address")
@NotEmpty
private String address;

@Column(name = "city")
@NotEmpty
private String city;

@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Phone number must be in E.164 form")
private String telephone;

@Column(name = "email")
private String email;

@Column(name = "registration_date")
private LocalDate registrationDate;

@Column(name = "customer_code")
private String customerCode;

@Column(name = "household_id")
private String householdId;
```

Standard getters/setters exist for all, including `getAddress()/setAddress()`, `getHouseholdId()/setHouseholdId()`. Note: the JPA `@NotEmpty` on `address` is a persistence-layer bean-validation constraint, distinct from the pipeline validation in item 3.

## 2. Owner creation logic — OfficeFloor pipeline

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** defines the create pipeline. Step order (each `govern: [transaction]` from `unique` onward):

1. `normalize` → `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`
2. `normalizeEmail` → `NormalizeOwnerEmail`
3. `validate` → `ValidateOwnerFields`
4. `unique` → `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone`
5. `uniqueHousehold` → `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`
6. `build` → `BuildOwner`
7. `assignHousehold` → `AssignOwnerHousehold`
8. `defaultRegistrationDate` → `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`
9. `assignCustomerCode` → `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`
10. `save` → `SaveOwner`
11. `respond` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated`

Important: **there is NO address-normalization step in this pipeline** — only telephone and email are normalized. Address flows through unmodified.

Function classes (all under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`):

**`BuildOwner.java`** — maps the validated DTO to an `Owner` entity:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
    built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
}
```

**`SaveOwner.java`**:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

## 3. Required-field validation (incl. `address`)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`** — this is the "address must not be blank" check. Required fields (in report order): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`:

```java
private static Map<String, Supplier<String>> requiredFields(OwnerFieldsDto request) {
    Map<String, Supplier<String>> fields = new LinkedHashMap<>();
    fields.put("firstName", request::getFirstName);
    fields.put("lastName", request::getLastName);
    fields.put("address", request::getAddress);
    fields.put("city", request::getCity);
    fields.put("telephone", request::getTelephone);
    return fields;
}

public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, Validator validator,
        Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated) throws InvalidOwnerFieldsException {
    Set<String> invalid = new LinkedHashSet<>();
    requiredFields(request).forEach((name, accessor) -> {
        String value = accessor.get();
        if (value == null || value.isBlank()) {
            invalid.add(name);
        }
    });
    for (ConstraintViolation<OwnerFieldsDto> violation : validator.validate(request)) {
        invalid.add(violation.getPropertyPath().toString());
    }
    if (!invalid.isEmpty()) {
        throw new InvalidOwnerFieldsException(new ArrayList<>(invalid));
    }
    validated.set(request);
}
```

A blank/missing field → `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` → 400. The exception (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/InvalidOwnerFieldsException.java`) carries the field-name list; handled by `InvalidOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler.java` and wired via `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.InvalidOwnerFieldsException.yml`.

Note the ordering constraint (from the YAML comments and `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`): since `address` currently is not normalized, a `"   "` (whitespace) address reaches `ValidateOwnerFields` unchanged and `isBlank()` catches it → 400. This matches the `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize` test.

## 4. Household duplicate detection

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold.java`** — compares `lastName + address` against all existing owners:

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException {
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return; // caller acknowledges the shared household
    }
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (Household.same(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress(),
                existing.getLastName(), existing.getAddress())) {
            throw new DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException(request.getLastName());
        }
    }
}
```

Supporting classes:
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException.java`** — carries `lastName`, message `"Owner household already in use: " + lastName`.
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateOwnerHouseholdExceptionHandler.java`** — responds 409 Conflict, detail `"An owner with this last name already lives at this address"`.
- Wired via **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException.yml`**.

## 5. Shared household id logic

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Household.java`** — the canonical-key + id computation (this is where address is canonicalized: trim, collapse internal whitespace to single space, lowercase):

```java
final class Household {
    private Household() {}

    static String key(String lastName, String address) {
        return canonical(lastName) + "\n" + canonical(address);
    }

    static boolean same(String lastNameA, String addressA, String lastNameB, String addressB) {
        return key(lastNameA, addressA).equals(key(lastNameB, addressB));
    }

    static String id(String lastName, String address) {
        return sha256Hex(key(lastName, address));
    }

    private static String canonical(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }

    private static String sha256Hex(String value) {
        try {
            byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(value.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(digest.length * 2);
            for (byte b : digest) {
                sb.append(String.format("%02x", b));
            }
            return sb.toString();
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 not available", e);
        }
    }
}
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerHousehold.java`** — assigns the id (only when `sharesHousehold=true`) and backfills existing household members:

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return; // only owners joining an existing household get a shared id
    }
    String householdId = Household.id(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (Household.same(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress(),
                existing.getLastName(), existing.getAddress())
                && !householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId())) {
            existing.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(existing);
        }
    }
}
```

## 6. Existing tests

Test tree is minimal — only an acceptance harness plus one test class:
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`**
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** (base harness)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java`

`AcceptanceTest.java` header comment: `address-normalize: Introduce address normalization applied whenever an owner is created: trim and collapse wh...`. Its three tests target **address normalization on create** (a feature not yet implemented in the pipeline):

```java
@Test void coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase() {
    o.put("address", "  12  main  st ");
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.address").value("12 MAIN STREET"));   // whitespace collapse + uppercase + "st"->"STREET"
}
@Test void functionalityExpandsAbbreviations() {
    o.put("address", "7 elm ave");
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.address").value("7 ELM AVENUE"));     // "ave"->"AVENUE"
}
@Test void errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize() {
    o.put("address", "   ");
    createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());                       // blank after normalize -> 400
}
```

The tests read address back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and expect an **uppercased, whitespace-collapsed, abbreviation-expanded** value (`st→STREET`, `ave→AVENUE`). There is currently no code producing this output — no `NormalizeOwnerAddress` class and no address step in `owners.POST.yml`. `AcceptanceBase` provides helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully valid unique owner), `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`, `getOwner`, `uniqueAddress()` (returns `seq() + " Test Street"`), plus `sha256hex`/`shaHex` helpers that mirror the `Household.id` algorithm. There are **no dedicated tests for household duplicate detection or household id** beyond what the `Household` code implements.

## 7. OwnerRequest / OwnerResponse DTOs and address flow

There are no hand-written `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse` classes. The DTOs are **OpenAPI-generated** from **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**:

- **`OwnerFieldsDto`** (generated from schema `OwnerFields`, lines ~1991-2060) — the request/input DTO. Fields: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (`minLength: 1`, `maxLength: 255`, example `'110 W. Liberty St.'`), `city`, `telephone`, `email`, `registrationDate`, and `sharesHousehold` (boolean, `writeOnly: true` — "not stored or returned"). `required: [firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone]`.
